Yes. Based on your spreadsheet and the **Custom threshold** screen you are using, below is how I would configure the rules.

One correction to your current Memory test: **25% is only suitable for testing**. For the production requirement in your sheet, Memory should be **Warning >85% and Critical >90%**.

Also, because your spreadsheet requires **Warning after 2 consecutive runs and Critical after 3 consecutive runs**, use **separate Warning and Critical rules**. Kibana supports a warning threshold in the same Custom Threshold rule, but the consecutive-run/alert-delay setting applies at rule level, so separate rules are cleaner when Warning and Critical require different consecutive counts. ([Elastic][1])

### Rule configuration

| Rule                                       | Rule type                            | Aggregation / field                 |           Threshold | Lookback | Check every | Consecutive runs | Group alerts by                                                           |
| ------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------- | ------------------: | -------: | ----------: | ---------------: | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `SP - CPU Utilisation - Warning`           | Custom threshold                     | MAX `system.cpu.total.norm.pct`     |                >80% |   10 min |       1 min |                2 | `labels.SPEN_Website`, `host.hostname`                                    |
| `SP - CPU Utilisation - Critical`          | Custom threshold                     | MAX `system.cpu.total.norm.pct`     |                >95% |   10 min |       1 min |                3 | Same                                                                      |
| `SP - Memory Utilisation - Warning`        | Custom threshold                     | MAX `system.memory.actual.used.pct` |                >85% |   10 min |       1 min |                2 | Same                                                                      |
| `SP - Memory Utilisation - Critical`       | Custom threshold                     | MAX `system.memory.actual.used.pct` |                >90% |   10 min |       1 min |                3 | Same                                                                      |
| `SP - Filesystem Usage - Warning`          | Custom threshold                     | MAX `system.filesystem.used.pct`    |                >85% |   10 min |       1 min |                2 | `labels.SPEN_Website`, `host.hostname`, preferably filesystem/mount field |
| `SP - Filesystem Usage - Critical`         | Custom threshold                     | MAX `system.filesystem.used.pct`    |                >90% |   10 min |       1 min |                3 | Same                                                                      |
| `SP - Application Availability - Warning`  | Synthetics monitor status            | Monitor status DOWN                 |   Failure condition |   15 min |       5 min |                2 | Monitor                                                                   |
| `SP - Application Availability - Critical` | Synthetics monitor status            | Monitor status DOWN                 |   Failure condition |   15 min |       5 min |                3 | Monitor                                                                   |
| `SP - SQL Server Service - Warning`        | Elasticsearch query/custom threshold | SQL service stopped condition       | Service unavailable |    5 min |       1 min |                2 | Host                                                                      |
| `SP - SQL Server Service - Critical`       | Elasticsearch query/custom threshold | SQL service stopped condition       | Service unavailable |    5 min |       1 min |                3 | Host                                                                      |

Kibana Custom Threshold supports `MAX` aggregation and grouping by one or more fields; each unique combination becomes a separate alert. ([Elastic][1])

